  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elbitamerica is the vendor listed with $389M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Elbitamerica recorded 214 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.8M and obligations up 399.6% year over year. Elbitamerica received the bulk of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $334M. Elbitamerica also sold to the Department of Defense, which obligated $54.9M, while the Department of Transportation shows $0 in obligations. Elbitamerica’s largest market in FY2026 to date is Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing, with $344M in obligations. Elbitamerica has smaller obligations across machinery, aircraft parts, repair and maintenance, and electronics NAICS lines, including $14.4M in All Other Miscellaneous General Purpose Machinery Manufacturing and $11M in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did Elbitamerica’s obligations rise year over year?",
        "body": "Elbitamerica’s obligations rose 399.6% year over year in FY2026 to date. Elbitamerica’s FY2026 total of $389M is materially larger than the prior fiscal years shown, where FY25 was $77.9M and FY24 was $137M. Elbitamerica’s concentration of obligations from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $334M, explains most of the increase."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where does Elbitamerica sell most of its products to the federal government?",
        "body": "Elbitamerica sells most to the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $334M in FY2026 to date. Elbitamerica’s largest market is Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing, with $344M in obligations. Elbitamerica also has sales to the Department of Defense, which obligated $54.9M, and smaller amounts in NAICS markets such as All Other Miscellaneous General Purpose Machinery Manufacturing at $14.4M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $11M."
      }
    ]
